{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1108448-auspice-gifts-and-renown-raises-question","id":1108448,"title":"Auspice Gifts and Renown Raises Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-27T10:55:31-07:00","id":1108448,"title":"Auspice Gifts and Renown Raises Question","content":"Hello, everyone!<br /> <br /> I have a question about Gifts. In the book it is written:<br /> <br /> &quot;A character learns a Facet of the appropriate Renown when she gains a dot in that Renown; this costs no Experiences.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A werewolf always has one Moon Gift associated with her auspice. She gains the appropriate Facet every time she gains a dot in her auspice Renown without spending any further Experiences.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that:<br /> <br /> A) When you raise your Auspice Renown the appropriate Facet they mention is the Auspice Gift's power of that level (Cunning is raised to 3, you get New Moon Gift 3).<br /> <br /> B) When you raise your Auspice Renown the appropriate Facet they mention is a Shadow Gift Facet of Cunning from your Affinity Lists, ON TOP of the New Moon Gift at the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> C) None of the above<br /> <br /> Please help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T11:35:23-07:00","id":1108455,"title":"","content":"I believe it is 'B', but your wording about the appropriate facet stuff is off and confusing the matter. When you raise your Auspice Renown, you get the Moon Gift facet automatically (that is the appropriate facet it is talking about), and the other stuff you'd normally get, like a Facet of a shadow gift.<br /> <br /> I assume this is the incentive and only real benefit to raising what is supposed to be your 'core' renown. Otherwise there is no real benefit to raising it over the others.<br /> <br /> From the book, page 99, under Renown--<br /> <br /> &quot;As your character increases in Renown, she also increases<br /> her Gift dice pools and hunter\u2019s aspect rolls, and she also<br /> gains Facets of her Gifts. Each time your character increases<br /> her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift.<br /> Every time she increases any Renown, she gains a Facet of a<br /> Shadow or Wolf Gift. Her total Renown also determines her<br /> effective Spirit Rank (p. 183), according to the chart below.&quot;<br /> <br /> Specifically --&gt; &quot;Each time your character increases her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every time she increases any Renown, she gains a Facet of a Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seems to make it rather clear you get both. It's the benefit to raising your auspice Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1796-tempest","name":"Tempest","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T11:36:59-07:00","id":1108457,"title":"","content":"B. When an Irraka raises Cunning, sbe gets a Cunning Facet of one of her Shadow Gifts, AND she gets the next dot of her Moon Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T11:39:06-07:00","id":1108460,"title":"","content":"B. This kind of inquire pops every two weeks in the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}